233	  <section class="reveal">
234	    <h2>Try it both ways</h2>
235	    <p class="sec">With the tracing code as released, cutting the connection or crashing the agent lights the DISAGREE light: neatlogs records <b>SUCCESS</b> on a run that crashed. Flip the switch to Trueup's fixes and do it again: the record says <b>ERROR</b> and the light turns green: <b>AGREE</b>. Live tally from every visitor today and before:</p>
236	    <div class="cards" id="tally"></div>
237	  </section>
238	
239	  <section class="reveal">
240	    <h2>Where the fixes went</h2>
241	    <p class="sec">Trueup found the cause in the tracing code, wrote each fix with tests, and sent them upstream. "With Trueup's fixes" above runs exactly these. They are proposals until merged.</p>
242	    <div class="cards">
243	      <div class="proof"><div class="label">Arize · OpenInference #4024</div><img src="/x/1-arize-review.png" alt="Arize's head of open source reviewing the pull request" loading="lazy"><h3>Reviewed by Arize's head of open source</h3><p>"Making a failed run show up on the root span is the right goal." We applied his changes; 300 tests pass. neatlogs runs this same code for AI agents, so one fix repairs both.</p><a href="https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference/pull/4024" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the pull request →</a><span class="prov">How this fix was made: <a href="https://entire.io/gh/Jennycruzy/trueup/commit/79210a45418246ceb95e2990d1c003b5fbc7b3d9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Entire record →</a></span></div>
244	      <div class="proof"><div class="label">neatlogs #207</div><img src="/x/3-neatlogs-pr.png" alt="The pull request sent to neatlogs" loading="lazy"><h3>Sent to neatlogs</h3><p>neatlogs' own agent recorder had the same bug. The fix comes with 6 tests: 2 fail without it, all pass with it. Their full test suite still passes.</p><a href="https://github.com/neatlogs/neatlogs/pull/207" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the pull request →</a><span class="prov">Recorded build: <a href="https://entire.io/gh/Jennycruzy/trueup/commit/79210a45418246ceb95e2990d1c003b5fbc7b3d9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Entire record →</a></span></div>
245	      <div class="proof"><div class="label">neatlogs' own email</div><div class="big"><span class="g" id="c1">6.2</span>% <span style="color:var(--dim)">→</span> <span class="r" id="c2">11.1</span>%</div><h3>The daily email got it wrong</h3><p>neatlogs' email said 6.2% of our runs failed. We checked all 81: 9 had crashed, 11.1%. These were test runs we crashed on purpose; the tracing code missed the crashes, and the email added up what it was given.</p><a href="https://github.com/Jennycruzy/trueup/blob/main/docs/neatlogs-email.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Every run, by ID →</a></div>
246	    </div>
247	  </section>
248	
249	  <section class="reveal two" style="margin-top:64px">
250	    <div>
251	      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Add the second sensor</h2>
252	      <p class="sec">Two lines in your agent. Witness never changes what your app does, never sends prompt or reply text beyond what neatlogs already records, and turns off with <code>TRUEUP_WITNESS=0</code>. Across 40 normal real calls it raised zero false alarms.</p>
253	    </div>
254	    <div class="code" id="code"><button class="copy" id="copy">Copy</button><span class="k">import</span> trueup.witness
255	trueup.witness.<span class="f">watch</span>()</div>
